{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And words of</b> — it lacks a bet; [read] ובדברי (\"and with words of\"), like כי ששת ימים (Exodus 20:10). Or it is figurative, for words surrounded him." "<b>They fight me</b> — וילחמו עמי (\"they fought with me\") חנם (\"without cause\"), like לא יגורך רע — לא יגור עמך רע (Psalms 91:10)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 109, :notes {0 "The second option reads the lack of bet as deliberate metaphor rather than deficiency.", 1 "The citation reads לא יגורך in one witness where the biblical text has לא תאונה; translated exactly as Ibn Ezra quotes it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:10.649570050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}